<title>BOTSWANA: Botswana Insurance yr shr jumps to profit.</title>
<headline>Botswana Insurance yr shr jumps to profit.</headline>
<dateline>GABORONE 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yr ended March 31, 1997</p>
<p>		    (million pula unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (thebe)			    20.5    vs  2.1 loss</p>
<p>    Div (thebe)			    12	vs  10</p>
<p>    Income				   4.33    vs  0.42 loss</p>
<p>    Total net premium income	   139.82  vs  124.13</p>
<p>    Pre-tax income			 5.94    vs  0.63</p>
<p>    Tax					1.51    vs  1.05</p>
<p>Full name: Botswana Insurance Holdings Limited</p>
<p>Note - The company said it will award capitalisation shares in the ratio of 4.2 new shares for every 100 shares held at an issue price of 1.90 pula per share.</p>
<p>It said its two major shareholders Africa Life Assurance Company (31.6 percent) and U.S. firm St Paul Insurance (25 percent) have elected to receive capitalisation shares.</p>
<p>The group's life division had more than doubled shareholders surplus before tax this year to 5.7 million pula from 2.5 million pula in 1996 and was well positioned for consistent and profitable growth.</p>
<p>-- Gaborone newsroom +267 347182</p>
</text>
